<exercise>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Different colors of light waves travell with different speeds in transparent medium. How they travell in vacuum?
        <ol marker="I">
          <li>At different speeds.</li>
          <li>At same speed. </li>
            <li>Both a and b. </li>
              <li>None of the above.</li>
            </ol>
      </p>
    </statement>
    </exercise>

    <exercise>
    <statement>
      <p>
        My radio station is tuned at 90MHz frequency. What is the wavelength of that radio wave.
        The velocity of electromagnetic wave is <m>3\times 10^8 m/s.</m>
        </p>
    </statement>
    <solution>
       <p> Given: <m>f=90MHz= 90\times 10^6 Hz</m>, <m>v= 3\times 10^8 m/s,</m>, <m>\Lambda=?</m>
        <md>
          <mrow>v \amp =f\lambda </mrow>
           <mrow>\lambda \amp =\frac{v}{f} </mrow>
           <mrow>\lambda \amp =\frac{3\times 10^8}{90\times 10^6} </mrow>
           <mrow>\therefore \lambda \amp =3.33 m </mrow>
        </md>
      </p>
    </solution>
    </exercise>


</exercises>




